    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 acceptance tests green, including both the default-to-today and keep-supplied-date cases).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec: when no registration date is supplied on `POST /api/owners`, default it to the server's current date, and expose `registrationDate` as an ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` string.\n\nTo keep structural impact low, I added behaviour as small cohesive units rather than touching any large method:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 new `registrationDate` field (`LocalDate`) with a trivial getter/setter (CC 1 each) and a small `@PrePersist` hook (CC 2) that fills in `LocalDate.now()` only when the field is null. No existing method was modified.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain a `LocalDate` field. Jackson serializes it as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\nNotably I did **not** touch `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` or `OwnerMapper`: MapStruct auto-maps the same-named `registrationDate` property in both directions, and the `@PrePersist` default runs at save time (after mapping), so the supplied value is preserved when present and defaulted when absent. The two hot paths (a large controller method and the mapper interface) stayed untouched.",
